WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.295
Lesson 10.7.

00:00:02.295 --> 00:00:05.310
Being the house: perp-exchange liquidity vaults.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.302
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:07.302 --> 00:00:09.886
able to understand what you're really taking on

00:00:09.886 --> 00:00:12.685
when you provide liquidity to a perpetuals exchange.

00:00:13.985 --> 00:00:15.275
Here's the plan.

00:00:15.275 --> 00:00:16.960
First, the key ideas.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.675
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:19.675 --> 00:00:21.200
Then, your checklist.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.362
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:24.662 --> 00:00:27.594
Many on-chain perp exchanges let you deposit

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:29.940
into a liquidity vault that acts as

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.977
the counterparty to traders (the "house").

00:00:32.977 --> 00:00:36.757
The vault earns trading fees, borrowing/funding fees and

00:00:36.757 --> 00:00:40.307
part of liquidations, and loses when traders win.

00:00:40.307 --> 00:00:44.968
First, Returns: fees + traders' losses − traders' profits.

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:48.083
Next, Risks: a run of profitable traders (or

00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:51.613
a few very large ones), open interest concentrated

00:00:51.613 --> 00:00:55.005
on one side, oracle manipulation or latency, the

00:00:55.005 --> 00:00:59.020
market-making strategy of the vault (some vaults actively

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:01.743
trade), and exchange contract risk.

00:01:01.743 --> 00:01:05.996
And finally, Check: the vault's historical P&L split (fees

00:01:05.996 --> 00:01:09.888
vs trader P&L), its open-interest caps, how it prices

00:01:09.888 --> 00:01:13.924
assets (oracle), and withdrawal rules (cooldowns, fees).

00:01:15.225 --> 00:01:17.740
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:21.713
A vault shows 25% APR: 18% from fees, 7%

00:01:21.713 --> 00:01:26.665
from traders' net losses over the last 6 months.

00:01:26.665 --> 00:01:30.581
In a strong one-directional trend, traders who are long

00:01:30.581 --> 00:01:34.288
win, so the vault's "trader P&L" component can swing

00:01:34.288 --> 00:01:37.245
to −20% or worse, wiping out the fees.

00:01:37.245 --> 00:01:39.572
Size it as an active trading exposure,

00:01:39.572 --> 00:01:41.900
not as fixed income, and check whether

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.929
withdrawals are delayed in stress.

00:01:45.228 --> 00:01:47.926
Trader skill and trending markets; oracle

00:01:47.926 --> 00:01:50.625
quality; the exchange's own risk controls.

00:01:51.926 --> 00:01:53.386
Here's your checklist.

00:01:53.386 --> 00:01:54.921
Do it now, for real.

00:01:54.921 --> 00:01:57.531
First, Vault returns split into fees

00:01:57.531 --> 00:01:59.806
vs trader P&L, with history.

00:01:59.806 --> 00:02:03.261
Next, Open-interest caps and oracle design reviewed.

00:02:03.261 --> 00:02:06.641
And finally, Withdrawal cooldowns and stress behaviour known.

00:02:07.941 --> 00:02:09.151
Question 1.

00:02:09.151 --> 00:02:11.236
When does a perp liquidity vault lose money?

00:02:15.656 --> 00:02:17.863
The answer: When traders are net

00:02:17.863 --> 00:02:20.136
profitable, e.g. in strong trends.

00:02:21.436 --> 00:02:22.681
Question 2.

00:02:22.681 --> 00:02:24.186
Why isn't it fixed income?

00:02:28.606 --> 00:02:30.628
The answer: Part of the return is

00:02:30.628 --> 00:02:33.186
traders' losses, which can reverse sharply.

00:02:34.486 --> 00:02:35.756
Question 3.

00:02:35.756 --> 00:02:38.166
Name two things to check before depositing.

00:02:42.466 --> 00:02:46.278
The answer: Any two: fee vs trader-P&L history,

00:02:46.278 --> 00:02:50.726
OI caps, oracle design, withdrawal rules, contract risk.

00:02:52.026 --> 00:02:53.271
Let's recap.

00:02:53.271 --> 00:02:57.534
Returns: fees + traders' losses − traders' profits.

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:59.846
Risks: a run of profitable traders

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.929
(or a few very large ones).

00:03:01.929 --> 00:03:05.422
Check: the vault's historical P&L split (fees

00:03:05.422 --> 00:03:08.384
vs trader P&L), its open-interest caps.

00:03:09.684 --> 00:03:12.199
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:12.199 --> 00:03:14.857
Next up, Lesson 10.8: DeFi rates:

00:03:14.857 --> 00:03:17.514
term structure, fixed vs floating.
